  <!-- Chapter 11 -->
  <ChapterCard
    id="ch11"
    number={11}
    title="Gran Plain (Standard Chapter 1)"
    code="GRAN1"
    timeline="Standard"
  >
    <TacticalBriefing
      level="14"
      party="Stocke, Raynie, Marco"
      
      enemies={[{"name": "Blue Flame", "weakness": "Ice"}, {"name": "Goblin Foot", "weakness": "Lightning"}, {"name": "Wood Goblin", "weakness": "Lightning"}]}
    />

    <div class="chapter-walkthrough-prose">
<p>Gran          There&#x27;s no treasure here either, so just head north to the    Plain E        Gran Plain East, and west to the checkpoint.  Yet again,    _______        you&#x27;ll be distracted by someone in distress back east.   |       |       Make sure to choose &quot;Let&#x27;s go save her now.&quot;, as this is a   |       |       requirement to unlocking the [At Journey&#x27;s End] sidequest   |__   __|       later.  Either way, you&#x27;ll have to deal with the source of   ___| |__        the disturbance.     S     |   _       |       *************************************************************    \     /        BOSS TIME: Sabertooth Tiger x2     \   /         WEAKNESS: None      | |          STRATEGY: Have Marco cast Magic Boost on Raynie, while Stocke 			and she Push Assault the tigers into the back row.  Then, use      | |__        two combos of Left Assault, any spell, and an attack from     /     |       Marco to finish them off quickly.    /    __|       *************************************************************   |    |___   |        |      For defeating them, you will meet Aht, Liese, and Vanoss, all   |     ___|      Beastkind of the Satyros, and the former of which who will   |    |          join your party.  I would recommend handing Stocke&#x27;s Beast                   Skins down to Aht, as I&#x27;m going to purchase something new for Gran Plain SE     him soon enough, anway.</p>

<Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Beastkind">
<p>Now, return west to the checkpoint where you have another decision to make. Choosing to &quot;Force your way through&quot; will unlock [A Sealed Path] ending.</p>
</Callout>

<Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Stocke&#x27;s Display">
<p>Return to this node, even though trying to &quot;Abandon the idea&quot; will only lead to a dead end for now.</p>
</Callout>

<Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Sword Dancing">
<p>There&#x27;s nothing we can do here for now.  If you have already resolved this roadblock, then skip to GRAN2.  Otherwise, this would be a good time to wrap up some sidequests.</p>
</Callout>

<p>Return to &quot;The Beginning&quot; node and choose to Join the Rosch Brigade.  If you have at least 5300 G, then go ahead and buy a Custom Lance for Rosch.  Head down to the first ward and give the two Anti-Sleeps you purchased earlier to the soldier on the left to complete the [Night Watch] sidequest and receive the Alistel Edge (ATK+16/MAG+6, equip on Marco).</p>

<p>Continue on with the plot as before and return to the site of the cave-in.  For those who don&#x27;t remember, go west and south one screen.  Then, hug the river clockwise until it turns north to where you met the spy in Standard History. At this point, the soldier is still alive, so use the barrel to blow away the rocks.  Talk to the soldier to complete the [Accident in the Cave] sidequest and receive the Right-Cut Scroll for Marco, though you can&#x27;t use it for now. You can either walk to Alma Mine or use Historia to skip ahead to [The Closed Mine] node.</p>

<p>=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=</p>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

  <!-- Chapter 12 -->
