<p>Go right to the fork, up, and left to find a barrel.  Pull it to the right to blow up the rocks over there.  After a cutscene, head left to a room with a chest which contains 800G.  Return to where you blew up the rock, and walk up to the next area.</p>

<p>Take either path around to a save point.  Go left to a couple barrels.  Pull one of them back, so you don&#x27;t end up blowing them both up at the same time. You&#x27;ll need both of them to get through the boulders.  To the left is a chest which contains 4 ROYAL JELLIES.  Blow up the boulders and pull one of the barrels to the right to blow up some more.  Follow the path to the right to a chest which contains a HEALING HERB.</p>

<p>You may want to return to the save point to heal up and/or use some Royal Jellies on Raynie.  For the next part, if you&#x27;re not going to use Raynie, then give her Horn Charms to Stocke.  In either case, you will reach the end of the mine to the north, and find what you were looking for.</p>

<p>******************************************************************************* BOSS TIME: Granorg Archer x3, Light Granorgite x4 WEAKNESS: None STRATEGY: You&#x27;ll definitely want Marco for this fight, starting by casting Magic Boost on your primary magic user for this fight.  Any combination of Assaults and a spell should be able to take them out.  Otherwise, maybe casting Guard Boost would be a good idea with so many of them around.  They&#x27;re not particularly dangerous, if you&#x27;ve been following the walkthrough up to now. *******************************************************************************</p>

<p>Afterwards, everyone returns home to Alistel after a job well done.</p>

<p>=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=</p>
