<p>S - Save Point     X - Obstacle     1 - Wisp Blade     2 - Herbal Tea x2</p>

<p>Walk along the western edge of the Sand Fortress South area to avoid any hidden traps up the middle.  Enter the Fortress and report to Viola.</p>

<Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: The Valkyrie">
<p>First, go outside and buy two Knight Studs from the merchant for Marco.  It&#x27;s not a big upgrade at all, but you should have plenty of money to spend.  You&#x27;ll find something better later, which is why I say only buy two. Rosch &amp; Viola are in the upper middle room on the first floor, but I recommend checking out the rest of the fortress first.</p>
</Callout>

<p>Walk up the middle of the first floor to the second floor.  In the left room above, you can rest up in a bed for free.  Outside the room, you can find Kiel training to the left.  Talk to him to learn sword-dancing from him and upgrade your Strike ability to be able to cut down tall grass.  Return to the stairs and continue up to the third floor.</p>

<p>Head around to the right, up the stairs, and proceed up to go outside to the Sand Fortress North area.  In the upper left area is some tall grass that you can now cut down to access two chests which contains 2 HERBAL TEAS and the WISP BLADE (ATK+18/MAG+12/HP+50, equip on Marco).</p>

<p>Return to the first floor, walk around to the right and into the upper middle room.  Talk to Viola first to advance the [A Letter to Tomorrow] sidequest. Then, talk to Rosch and go with him to inform the brigade of your new orders. As the battle begins, you will have another decision to make.  Choosing to &quot;Send reinforcements&quot; will unlock the [Front of Despair] ending.</p>

<Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Conditions Worsen">
<p>Return to &quot;The Valkyrie&quot; and advance the plot up to the same decision. However, choosing to &quot;Prioritize the mission&quot; will only lead to a dead end.</p>
</Callout>

<Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Ambush Tactics">
<p>If you have already resolved this roadblock, then skip to SAND3.  Otherwise, this would be a good time to put that sword-dancing skill to use.  I would recommend waiting until later to use it at Lazvil Hills.  Instead, return to &quot;Stocke&#x27;s Display&quot; node in Standard History.</p>
</Callout>

<Callout type="note" title="Recommended Equipment">
<p>Recommended Equipment at this point in the game<br/>Stocke: Rune Edge, Silver Mail, Fang Charm x3<br/>Raynie: Rune Spear, Silver Mail, Horn Charm x3<br/>Marco: Wisp Blade, Heavy Mail, Knight Stud x2, Pawn Stud<br/>Rosch: P.Thauma Spear, Silver Mail, Fang Charm x3</p>
</Callout>

<p>=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=</p>
