<p>If you have already learned sword-dancing, then you can continue with the plot from here.  Before doing so, head north of the save point, and cut the tall grass to the east to gain access to a chest which contains a FIRST AID KIT. From the save point, head west to the decision from before and choose &quot;Abandon the idea&quot; to proceed onward this time.</p>

<p>Even though she&#x27;s a bit of a liability at this point, replace Raynie with Aht, as she could use the experience, and give her Raynie&#x27;s Horn Charms.  She can use elemental traps during battle.  The way they work is that you lay a trap on an empty tile, then move an enemy or group of enemies onto them for massive damage.  You can also set a trap on an enemy, if the tile was empty when you entered the command, and you moved the enemy onto the tile before laying the trap.  Since she doesn&#x27;t have any assaults right now, and she&#x27;s rather frail, it&#x27;s more trouble than it&#x27;s worth right now, but I&#x27;d still recommend using her for the experience.  Against Goblins, it may not be a bad idea to have her cast Polaris in a pre-emptive strike, to protect against poison.</p>

<p>To the northwest are some rocks, and a barrel above them.  You know what to do. Blow them up to access a chest which contains a BISHOP STUD (DEF+6/MDF+6, equip on Marco).  If you want, blow up the wood or rocks to the west and go west to Gran Plain West.</p>

<p>Before going south, cut the tall grass to the west to gain access to a chest which contains a HOLY WATER.  Then, head south to the Forest Clearing.  Go left of the save point to find a chest which contains 3 ANTI-POISONS.  Keep going south to where you will set up camp.</p>

<Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Collecting Wood">
<p>Return north and Aht will teach Stocke the Mana Sight ability that will let you see hidden objects, including the first of five WITHERED BRANCHES that you must find.  This includes the bombs back at the Sand Fortress.  If you want to go back there now, then skip to SAND3, but I wouldn&#x27;t do that.  Also, there is a lot of hidden treasure in previous areas that we could get now.  Again, I will wait until it is more convenient to do so.</p>
</Callout>

<Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Preparing a Meal">
<p>Go west and cut through the tall grass again.  In the upper right corner of the area, you will find a WITHERED BRANCH.  Head east to the central Gran Plan area and north to find another WITHERED BRANCH.  Proceed north to the Gran Plain Northwest area, and hug the east wall until you find yet another WITHERED BRANCH.  Follow Aht&#x27;s direction, and walk south two screens to the South Hill.</p>
</Callout>

<p>At this time, I would recommend switching Raynie in to replace Aht, as well as giving her back the Horn Charms.  Search by the tree on the right to find the last WITHERED BRANCH and something else will find you.</p>

<p>******************************************************************************* BOSS TIME: Fumble, Rare Mushroom WEAKNESSS: Poison, Fire STRATEGY: FINALLY!  A boss fight with elemental weaknesses we can exploit! Start with Marco&#x27;s Push Assault on Fumble, Fire from Stocke to also take out the mushroom, and Poison Break on Fumble.  In the next round, have Marco use Magic Boost on Raynie, Stocke uses Right Assault on the mushroom, and Raynie casts Fire on the two.  Once they&#x27;re all out of the way, I would use the Change command to string together six consecutive turns of alternating between physical attacks and spells to finish off the Fumble before he can call for more mushroom backup. *******************************************************************************</p>

<p>For defeating him, you will get some Fresh Meat for dinner.  Return to the Forest Clearing and talk to Vanoss or Liese to sleep the night there.  Aht will also give Stocke the White Page.  In the morning, use the save point to return to Historia.  With the White Page, Lippti and Teo will unlock your first Mana Burst: Turn Break, which can delete an enemy&#x27;s turn panel.  You can fill up the Mana Burst gauge by either dealing or receiving damage.</p>

<p>Now, we can begin heading to Granorg.  Head north, east, and north one screen to return to the Gran Plain Northwest area.  Continue north for a small scene.</p>

<Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: Aht&#x27;s Prayer">
<p>Afterwards, exit north to reach Granorg.  I would strongly recommend maxing out at least one characters&#x27; Mana Burst gauge for one of the upcoming sidequests.</p>
</Callout>

<Callout type="note" title="Recommended Equipment">
<p>Recommended Equipment at this point in the game<br/>Stocke: Rune Edge, Silver Mail, Fang Charm x3<br/>Raynie: Rune Spear, Silver Mail, Horn Charm x3<br/>Marco: Wisp Blade, Heavy Mail, Bishop Stud, Knight Stud x2<br/>Aht: Petty Knife, Beast Skins</p>
</Callout>

<p>=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=</p>
    </div>
  </ChapterCard>

