<p>S - Save Point    X - Inaccessible    1 - Anti-Paralytic    2 - Might Herb x2</p>

<Callout type="node" title="Historia Milestone: An Ancient City">
<p>Your contact is in the Commercial District to the east.  So naturally, we should head west first.  Follow the path north and west to Downtown Granorg. Go up the stairs to the inn where you should rest up.  In one of the rooms upstairs is a chest which contains an ANTI-PARALYTIC.</p>
</Callout>

<p>Leave the inn, go down the stairs to the shops, and talk to the man in green, named Hilster/Hilstar (typo in the game.  I&#x27;ll use Hilster) to receive [The Ultimate Dish] sidequest.  Talk to the merchant on the right to get some more information on conuts for the [What Was Inherited] sidequest, though I&#x27;m not sure if that&#x27;s a mandatory requirement.  If you continue west, you&#x27;ll find a tavern and a small alley behind it.</p>

<p>Return to the Main Street area and head east to the Commercial District. Stocke will point out your contact, but you should not talk to him just yet. Go right to the item shop, where just outside to the left of it, you will find a chest which contains 2 MIGHT HERBS.  Enter the item shop and talk to the merchant to advance [The King&#x27;s Daughter] sidequest.</p>

<p>Climb the stairs next to the item shop and head left to the equipment shop.  I would ignore the speed handicap and buy two Heavy Mails for Stocke &amp; Raynie. Afterwards, talk to the man in the robe below and between the two staircases.</p>

<Callout type="note" title="Recommended Equipment">
<p>Recommended Equipment at this point in the game<br/>Stocke: Rune Edge, Heavy Mail, Fang Charm x3<br/>Raynie: Rune Spear, Heavy Mail, Horn Charm x3<br/>Marco: Wisp Blade, Heavy Mail, Bishop Stud, Knight Stud x2</p>
</Callout>

<p>=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=</p>
